From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Tue, 18 Nov 2025 14:04:24 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: reserve a minimum of TX tokens per band

Multi-radio devices share one TX token pool among all bands, so one
busy band can take every token and stop TX on the other bands. A
fixed cap per band stops that, but also keeps a loaded band from the
tokens that idle bands leave unused.

Each band keeps a reserve of tokens. A band inside its reserve always
gets a token. A band over its reserve takes free tokens only beyond
the unused reserves of the other bands, and a frame it cannot place
is dropped instead of a TX block for all bands. On mt7915 with DBDC
the reserve is half of the pool, which keeps the ceiling of the cap.
The token records the station band apart from the queue band, because
the pending count of PSD frames must stay on the queue band: an MLO
station sends odd TIDs on its second link, and a frame of the global
wcid can use a queue on another band. A reset clears every band
count, because a stale count changes admission for all bands. The
debugfs knob token_reserve changes the reserve at run time; 0 turns
it off. On mt7996, debugfs shows the token state and the TXD and
frame of a selected token.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
